  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.6,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.6,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the $4.50 no-show cancellation fee was correctly charged and stands, and the driver is paid $3.60 compensation.\n\nWhy the fee stands. POL-NS-01 requires all four limbs and each holds. (a) The trip record EV-TRIP-02736 carries the driver's 'arrived' event, the 'I'm Here' tap at 13:24:34. (b) The GPS trace EV-GPS-02736 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius — 44 qualifying fixes running from 13:24:34, the same instant as the tap. (c) The driver held position inside the geofence for a continuous 428 seconds, from 13:24:34 to 13:31:42, well over the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180), measured as the clause requires from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the tap. (d) The trip record shows no boarding and no started_at/ended_at, and the driver terminated at 13:31:43 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the codes limb (d) recognises, after the required dwell had elapsed.\n\nNo displacing clause applies. POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) does not fire: the derived facts put the first qualifying in-geofence fix at exactly the tap time with dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0, so the marker is true and no recomputation or refund arises. POL-NS-06 (shortfall) does not fire: the measured dwell exceeds the minimum by 248 seconds (shortfall_sec -248.0), and the MISSING traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02736-01 (weight 0.0, no advisory covers this pickup) helps nobody because no accumulation of separate intervals is needed. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) does not apply — the driver's stationary fixes are inside, not outside, the arrival radius — and POL-NS-02's proximity test is satisfied. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider: the chat log EV-CHAT-02736 holds one message, sent by the driver at 13:24:59, and no rider message at all, so limb (a) fails.\n\nThe amount. POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the fee in force: 0.80 x $4.50 = $3.60, matching the fare ledger's derived driver_compensation of $3.60. The anti-farming check does not trip — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the 'four or more' limb, and 2 divided by 64 completed_trips_30d is 0.031, below 0.08 — so compensation is paid, not withheld. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries the same $3.60, the amount the ruling moves; the rider's charge stands as it presently is (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd $0.00), so no refund is due on this rider-filed dispute. The monetary effect, $3.60, does not exceed the $8.00 automatic-execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so it executes on issue subject to the appeal route.\n\nWeight and confidence. The GPS trace EV-GPS-02736 is impaired at weight 0.85 with issue code GPS_GAP_SHORT_OR_OUTSIDE_WINDOW: a single 60-second sampling gap from 13:21:14 to 13:22:14. That gap sits before the waiting window opened and is under POL-NS-08(b)'s 120-second policy threshold, so it is schema-level impairment only — it does not engage POL-NS-08's escalation sentence and does not make the trace unusable. It is the artifact that measures the driver's position and dwell, so it caps confidence at 0.85 under POL-GEN-02(2), above the 0.70 floor. The finding survives the discount because the gap touches neither the arrival nor the dwell, and the trip record (EV-TRIP-02736, weight 1.0) independently records the arrival event, the wait timer and the cancellation. The rider's kept claim — that the trace's impairment must be disclosed and down-weights it — is correct and is accepted; it does not change the outcome.\n\nThe rider's assertion 'I was there' is not borne out by the record: the rider's own track within EV-GPS-02736 records 74 fixes, all stationary, none inside the 100 m rider-presence radius, some 760 m from the pin. That does not change the fee, because the rider's presence is not a condition of the charge, but it is why the dispute fails.\n\nNo escalation trigger fires (POL-NS-09): confidence is above the floor; no two artifacts contradict on arrival, dwell or rider presence; both parties' disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0; the anti-farming check does not trip and rider no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and the deciding fact is not carried solely by a policy-impaired artifact. No clause produces a referral. This ruling is provisional and either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
